Subject: [Wine 11.0] Preserve color semantic indices in shader disassembly.

Base: Wine 11.0, db11d0fe6a169c457e23d007e20404643d067aa8

3DMark06 Perlin Noise compiles, disassembles, and reassembles its shaders.
The Wine/vkd3d disassembler turns dcl_color1 into dcl_specular0, which is not
valid shader assembly. Wine's assembler rejects it with D3DXERR_INVALIDDATA.
Keep the COLOR usage and its original index, including indices above one.
This is a local fix, not an upstream backport.

Regression: tools/buildWine/probes/shader-color-roundtrip.c covers every
color index from 0 through 15 for VS 2 input, VS 3 input/output, and PS 3
input declarations. It requires byte-for-byte identical assembled bytecode
after disassembly/reassembly. The v18 Wine filesystem fails 60/64 cases.
Repeat the 3DMark06 Perlin Noise feature test after rebuilding Wine.

--- a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3d_asm.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3d_asm.c
@@ -516,14 +516,8 @@
             usage = "psize";
             break;
         case VKD3D_DECL_USAGE_COLOR:
-            if (semantic->usage_idx)
-            {
-                usage = "specular";
-                indexed = true;
-                --usage_idx;
-                break;
-            }
             usage = "color";
+            indexed = true;
             break;
         case VKD3D_DECL_USAGE_TEXCOORD:
             usage = "texcoord";
